an international search is underway for  donors with an extremely rare blood type  to help save a two-year-old Florida girl  battling aggressive cancer  Zainab Mughal was diagnosed with  neuroblastoma two months ago she has one  of the rarest blood types in the world  to fight her cancer she'll need a team  of doctors and at least seven donors  Niki batiste shows us the desperate  effort to find a match Niki good morning  good morning more than 1,000 donors have  been tested so far but only three  matches have been found  Zainab parents say her family members  are not a match and they are now all  pleading with people from around the  globe to donate blood whether it's  dancing or coloring Zainab Moo called  loves to have fun like most year olds  but three months ago her parents Rahil  and Maryam noticed something was wrong  why I said you know what I feel there's  something in the stomach and we should  go to the hospital doctors found an  aggressive form of cancer called  neuroblastoma and discovered Zainab  would need life-saving blood  transfusions I was just crying all the  time and what were they what happened to  my daughter and she is happy baby like  how could be this thing happening to her  Zainab is missing a common antigen most  people carry in their blood type called  Indian be the only people that can be a  match for her blood type are people of  100-percent Pakistani Indian or Iranian  descent but even within those  populations less than 4 percent are  missing the Indian B antigen  yesterday Zainab and her parents met  with a florida-based team from the  organization one blood who are leading  the search for donors the team has been  working around the clock and so far has  found a match in London and two in the  United States that won't be enough for  Zainab's treatments but her parents say  she is a fighter she is getting better  that's why we are getting better and we  are hoping every day and have very  strong faith she will make here so far  about 11,000 people have contacted one  blood saying they meet the criteria and  want to donate Zainab's parents are  asking people to give blood even if they  are not a match because it could help  others if you would like to donate or  find out if you are a match visit our  website at CBS this morning calm bianna  hopefully more people will be reaching  out after watching that Nikki thank you
 

